What Is the Compostable Packaging Market?
Compostable packaging consists of packaging materials designed to break down into non-toxic components under specified composting conditions. These materials include polylactic acid (PLA), starch-based compounds, cellulose-based materials, and other biopolymer blends.

Compostable packaging is used in food and beverage containers, flexible films, consumer goods packaging, agricultural applications, and selected medical and pharmaceutical products. Its adoption depends on material performance, recognized compostability standards, product certification, and access to suitable waste-processing infrastructure.

