Key Market Drivers
Increasing Demand for Sustainable Packaging
Growing environmental awareness is encouraging businesses to evaluate alternatives to conventional plastic packaging. Brand owners are incorporating compostable formats into selected product lines to address consumer expectations and sustainability objectives.

Regulatory Initiatives Targeting Packaging Waste
Governments and regulatory bodies are introducing policies focused on reducing packaging waste, improving material recovery, and strengthening environmental standards. These measures are encouraging packaging producers to develop certified materials and provide clearer information about end-of-life disposal.

Expansion of Foodservice and Flexible Packaging Applications
Foodservice businesses are exploring compostable cups, trays, bags, and takeaway containers for applications where food contamination can make conventional recycling difficult. Improvements in barrier performance and packaging functionality are helping broaden the range of potential uses.

